{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788269322,"nonce":"ePO3MGpHM7MhLFYi7MYGkX/3I6Y=","title":"Filed 2026-09-01 by the round that makes blueprints buildable, out of its","message":"\"resolve by investigation, do not queue\" pass. Deterministic, so it lands at the\nmod rung per DESIGN's 2026-09-01 ruling. Verified against the decompiled 1.6\nsource; cited by member.\n\n\n`grep Blueprint Source/AutoRimmer/` returns **zero hits**. Nothing in ~44 verbs\nand 34k lines reads a `Blueprint`, a `Frame`, `workDone`, `resourceContainer` or\n`TotalMaterialCost`. `digest`'s sections are time, site, alerts, colonists,\nresources, power, threats, changed — there is no construction section.\n\nSo the moment 3.3's `build` places a blueprint, the agent is blind to it. It\ncannot distinguish:\n\n- waiting for a hauler to bring steel,\n- fully stocked and waiting for a builder,\n- actively being worked,\n- finished,\n- cancelled, deconstructed or destroyed.\n\nThat is the exact shape of M1's invisible research bench one level up. M1's\nsymptom was `Alert_ColonistsIdle`; the cause the agent could not see was the\nstate of the thing it had asked for. A `build` verb without this read satisfies\nits own acceptance and still leaves the play loop unable to act.\n\n\nA finished build leaves **no blueprint and no frame**. `Blueprint.TryReplaceWithSolidThing`\nturns the blueprint into a `Frame` (`Blueprint_Build.MakeSolidThing` — note it\nalso calls `Map.enrouteManager.SendReservations`), and `Frame.CompleteConstruction`\nturns the frame into the building and destroys itself. So a poll that only\nenumerates live blueprints and frames reports \"finished\" and \"cancelled\"\nidentically, as nothing.\n\nTwo consequences the scope has to carry:\n\n1. **The read is keyed on a placement id**, which 3.3 already owes (\"every\n   placement journaled with a placement id\"). Given an id the read answers\n   blueprint / frame / built-thing / gone, and `gone` is further split by (2).\n2. **The transition is journaled as a positive event.** `Frame.CompleteConstruction(Pawn)`\n   and `Frame.FailConstruction(Pawn)` are both public and both are natural\n   Harmony postfix sites in exactly the idiom `JournalHooks.cs` already uses —\n   read-only, try/catch-swallowed, no `__result` writes. Without them, \"did my\n   build finish or did something cancel it\" is an inference from two absences.\n\n\n`Verse/ThingRequestGroup` has both `Blueprint` and `BuildingFrame`, so\n`map.listerThings.ThingsInGroup(...)` is the enumeration — no scanning.\n\n`RimWorld/Frame`:\n- `WorkToBuild` (`entityDefToBuild.GetStatValueAbstract(StatDefOf.WorkToBuild, Stuff)`),\n  `workDone`, `WorkLeft`, `PercentComplete` — the progress answer, exactly.\n- `resourceContainer` (`ThingOwner`), `TotalMaterialCost()`,\n  `ThingCountNeeded(ThingDef)`, `ThingCountNeededWithEnroute(ThingDef, Pawn)`,\n  `IsCompleted()` — the materials answer, including what is already hauled in\n  and what is en route.\n- `BuildDef`, `EntityToBuildStuff()`, `LabelEntityToBuild`.\n\n`RimWorld/Blueprint` / `Blueprint_Build`:\n- `TotalMaterialCost()`, `ThingCountNeeded(stuff)`, `SpaceRemainingFor(stuff)`,\n  `IsCompleted()`, `EntityToBuild()`, `EntityToBuildStuff()`, `stuffToUse`.\n- **`BlockingHaulableOnTop()`** — the game's own answer to \"why has nobody\n  started this\", and it is a public method, so the mod must not re-derive it.\n\n\n**1. `CostListAdjusted` is a memoizing static cache and both `TotalMaterialCost()`\nimplementations bottom out in it.** `RimWorld/CostListCalculator.CostListAdjusted(BuildableDef, ThingDef, bool)`\nholds `cachedCosts` keyed on `(entDef, stuff)` and populates on first read, plus\na `Reset()` whenever `Find.Storyteller.difficulty` changes. This is the\nlazy-init class DESIGN warns about — but it is def-level, process-lifetime, not\nscribed, and the game fills it on any construction-UI hover, so it is the same\nruling `c718e4a` reached for `BuildableDef.PlaceWorkers`: **acceptable, and the\ncode comment must say why.** Do not discover this a third time.\n\n**2. Reading material cost can EMIT A RED ERROR, which the suites count.**\n`CostListAdjusted` calls `Log.Error(\"Cannot get AdjustedCostList for ... with\nnull Stuff.\")` when `entDef.MadeFromStuff` and `stuff == null`, and again when\nstuff is passed for a def that is not `MadeFromStuff`.\n`Frame.ThingCountNeededWithEnroute` calls `Log.Error` twice more on negative or\nover-large amounts. `JournalHooks` postfixes `Log.Error` into the journal, and\nevery acceptance suite watermarks red errors — so a naive observer turns a clean\nrun red **by reading it**. Guard `stuffToUse == null` before asking, and decide\non-issue whether `WithEnroute` is worth the exposure or whether\n`enrouteManager.GetEnroute` should be read directly.\n\n**3. `Frame.WorkToBuild` is a `GetStatValueAbstract` call per frame per read.**\nFine for a handful; state a cap, in the shape `digest`'s other sections already\nuse (`cap` + `more`), rather than walking an unbounded list.\n\n\n**`construction {rect?|around?+radius?|placement_id?|id?}`** — a READ, observer\ndiscipline throughout.\n\nPer item: `{id, kind:\"blueprint\"|\"frame\", def, stuff, at, rot, footprint,\nplacement_id?, state, work_total, work_done, work_left, percent,\nmaterials:[{def, needed, present, enroute}], missing:[{def, count}],\nblocking_haulable:{def,label,at}|null, worker:{id,name}|null}`.\n\n`state` is the DONE-MEANS vocabulary and must be computed, not guessed:\n`awaiting-materials` (something in `missing`), `ready` (stocked, no worker),\n`in-progress` (a pawn's current job targets it), `blocked` (`BlockingHaulableOnTop`\nnon-null). A blueprint has no `workDone`; publish the work fields as absent\nrather than zero, so \"not started\" and \"0% done\" do not read alike.\n\nRollup: `{blueprints, frames, by_state:{...}, work_left_total, missing:[{def,count}],\ncap, more}`.\n\n**`digest.construction`** — small, capped, in the digest's idiom:\n`{blueprints, frames, awaiting_materials, blocked, work_left}`. This is what\nmakes an idle-colonist run diagnosable in one call instead of none.\n\n**Journal rows** for the two transitions, via Harmony postfix on\n`Frame.CompleteConstruction` and `Frame.FailConstruction`, carrying the\nplacement id where one is known.\n\n\n- With a blueprint placed and no materials on the map, `construction` lists it\n  with `state:\"awaiting-materials\"` and `missing` naming the def and count; the\n  same read after the materials are spawned reports `ready`.\n- After `advance`, the same item is a `frame` with `work_done \u003e 0`,\n  `percent` between 0 and 1, and `worker` naming the pawn doing it.\n- On completion the item is ABSENT from `construction`, a journal row records\n  the completion, and `construction {placement_id}` answers `built` naming the\n  resulting thing's id — not `gone`.\n- On `designate {type:\"cancel\"}` over the same cell, `construction {placement_id}`\n  answers `cancelled`, distinguishably from `built`, by field and not by\n  parsing a sentence.\n- A haulable item dropped on a blueprint makes `blocking_haulable` non-null and\n  `state:\"blocked\"`; removing it clears both.\n- **Zero red errors across the whole suite, including a deliberate read of a\n  blueprint of a `MadeFromStuff` def with null stuff** — the hazard-2 case. This\n  bullet is the one that proves the guard exists, so it is not optional.\n- `digest.construction` is present and its counts agree with `construction`'s\n  rollup on the same map state.\n- Shapes asserted per `accept/` convention: a missing key is a FAIL, never\n  `eq(None)`.\n\n\n`1adc737` (3.3 — this is the read its `build` is unusable without; the\nplacement id is its contract), `664e9b9` (M1: `Alert_ColonistsIdle` for the\nwhole run, and the research bench that could not be replaced), `2d9a1da`\n(colony sampling — same \"the harness records no rates\" family), `40ed42f`\n(work_coverage in the digest — same section, same cap idiom).","files":null}]}